WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.040
"Dexter" put out some seriously mind-blowing
episodes in its original 96-episode run, but

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.920
unfortunately, they can't all be good.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.350
These are the best and worst rated episodes
of the entire series, according to IMDb.

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:19.919
The finale of Season 4 remains a shocking
hour of television, featuring one of the most

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.939
tragic deaths in the entire series.

00:00:22.939 --> 00:00:27.980
Season 4 follows Dexter's pursuit of the Trinity
Killer, aka Arthur Mitchell, a church deacon

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.269
who uses building sites in ritualized murders.

00:00:31.269 --> 00:00:35.580
Initially, law enforcement only believes him
to have committed three murders.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.890
But in this episode, they discover a fourth
victim in a young boy who was kidnapped and

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:43.620
buried alive under the fresh concrete of church
housing.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:48.460
As if that's not enough, Dexter's mishandling
of Arthur Mitchell earlier in the season leads

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:53.230
to Trinity murdering Dexter's wife Rita, leaving
baby Harrison in her blood.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:58.320
While Arthur does end up on Dexter's slab,
the price isn't worth it.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.170
This is also the episode where Deb discovers
that Dexter is the Ice Truck Killer's brother,

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:06.310
which leads to her uncovering her brother's
real identity.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:09.280
It's no wonder this is considered one of the
best episodes of the show.

00:01:10.499 --> 00:01:15.499
One of the things that makes "Dexter" so powerful
is Dexter Morgan's ongoing relationship with

00:01:15.499 --> 00:01:20.729
his dead father, Harry, who acts as a ghostly
guide in many episodes.

00:01:20.729 --> 00:01:25.210
But in "Nebraska," Harry is replaced with
Dexter's brother Brian Moser, the Ice Truck

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:28.590
Killer, who encourages Dexter's worst impulses.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:31.759
It's uncomfortable to watch, and not in a
good way.

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:35.749
Dexter discovers the Trinity Killer's daughter,
Rebecca, killed herself in a bathtub, and

00:01:35.749 --> 00:01:38.899
his wife Sally has been found bludgeoned to
death.

00:01:38.899 --> 00:01:43.590
Assuming that the Trinity Killer's son, Jonah,
has taken up his father's mantle, Dexter drives

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:47.530
from Florida to Nebraska to confront Jonah
and kill him.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:51.869
But when he finds out that Rebecca killed
herself because of their mother's abuse and

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:56.420
Jonah beat his mother to death in retaliation,
Dexter lets Jonah live.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:01.270
Add in the convoluted Travis Marshall plot,
the entrance of Masuka's creepy Dexter-obsessed

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:06.610
intern Louis Greene, and Deb's odd relationship
drama, and this installment is a true flop.

00:02:07.999 --> 00:02:12.600
Season 1 of "Dexter" closes with a string
of horrifying reveals and events.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:17.200
In "Born Free," Deb has been kidnapped by
the Ice Truck Killer, Brian Moser, who also

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:21.379
happens to be her fiancé, under the name
Rudy Cooper.

00:02:21.379 --> 00:02:26.030
Dexter finds out that Brian is his brother,
and that Brian didn't get adopted alongside

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:30.510
him because Harry Morgan believed Brian would
grow up to be dangerously disturbed by his

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.120
memory of their mother's dismemberment.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.810
This turns out to be true: Brian has spent
a great deal of his life institutionalized,

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:41.720
before learning to hide his issues and start
a career in medicine.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:47.260
Not only is this an incredibly tense episode,
as Brian offers Deb to Dexter on a slab, it's

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:52.890
also key to Dexter's character development:
He chooses his adopted sister over his blood

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:53.890
brother.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:57.709
The episode ends with Dexter giving the Ice
Truck Killer a dose of his own medicine.

00:02:59.209 --> 00:03:04.950
It will surprise absolutely nobody that the
worst episodes of "Dexter" come almost entirely

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.659
from the final season.

00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:11.340
In this entry we get to know Zach Hamilton,
a would-be serial killer who murdered his

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.040
father's mistress and plans to kill his father
next.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.489
Dexter stops him and straps him to his table.

00:03:17.489 --> 00:03:22.090
But, as in "Nebraska," Dexter spares the boy
and decides to teach him Harry's code.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:27.090
This choice makes no sense in the show's broader
arc, since Zach is killed by the Brain Surgeon

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.709
just a few episodes later.

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:33.280
"A Little Reflection" also throws in a number
of clashing narrative arcs.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:37.829
Masuka flirts with his daughter, Deb's life
continues to disintegrate after murdering

00:03:37.829 --> 00:03:42.189
LaGuerta, and a new neighbor named Cassie
tries and fails to date Dexter.

00:03:42.189 --> 00:03:48.189
The first episode of Season 7 is a doozy that
marks the beginning of the end.

00:03:48.189 --> 00:03:52.719
Season 6 ends with Deb discovering Dexter
standing over Travis Marshall's body, about

00:03:52.719 --> 00:03:54.340
to stab him.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:59.379
Season 7 picks up in exactly that same moment,
as Dexter tries to explain away the grisly

00:03:59.379 --> 00:04:00.609
tableau.

00:04:00.609 --> 00:04:05.150
Deb doesn't believe him, but helps him set
a fire to cover up their involvement in Marshall's

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:06.540
death anyway.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:11.499
Eagle-eyed LaGuerta has been mildly suspicious
of Dexter for some time, and her Spidey-sense

00:04:11.499 --> 00:04:16.090
goes haywire when she finds a blood slide
at the scene of the crime matching the Bay

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:18.030
Harbor Butcher's MO.

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:22.630
By the end of the episode, Deb finds Dexter's
blood slides and asks him point blank,

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:27.280
"Are you a serial killer?"

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:30.139
"Yes."

00:04:30.139 --> 00:04:35.110
This is a vital moment in both Deb and Dexter's
narrative arcs, one that shapes new tragedies

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:36.110
on the way.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:41.060
You'd think that if you were an escaped and
most-wanted serial killer with a well-known

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:44.460
face, you'd stay away from the place you were
apprehended.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:47.990
If you must go back, you'd probably change
your appearance for protection.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:49.950
That's just common sense, right?

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:53.190
Well, here lies one of the many problems with
"Dress Code".

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:58.370
Hannah McKay is back and still wanted by the
police, yet she's done absolutely nothing

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.199
to disguise herself.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.300
She doesn't even bother to change her hair
color!

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.680
"Brave of her to be walking around Miami like
that."

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:10.480
It's a distractingly stupid detail, among
several others that make this convoluted episode

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.590
terrible.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:16.340
Deb gets deep into soap opera territory, as
it's clear her boss is in love with her and

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:18.030
acting like a jealous boyfriend.

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:22.830
Meanwhile, Deb's ex Quinn is pulling away
from his girlfriend Jamie, who is also Angel's

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.900
sister and Dexter's nanny.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:28.880
This web of relationships is uncomfortably
tangled, and only getting worse.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:36.600
The penultimate episode of Season 4 is a nailbiter,
as Arthur Mitchell quietly discovers who Kyle

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:42.669
Butler actually is: A Miami Metro PD blood
spatter analyst named Dexter Morgan.

00:05:42.669 --> 00:05:47.350
Suspicious that Kyle might not be who he says
he is, Arthur seeks out other Kyle Butlers

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:49.319
in town with murderous results.

00:05:49.319 --> 00:05:54.380
Eventually, the Trinity Killer casually strolls
through Miami Metro, even stopping to admire

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:58.670
the murder board chronicling all his crimes,
before coming face-to-face with Dexter and

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:02.380
calling him by his true name.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:06.199
"Hello, Dexter Morgan"

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:11.379
This is also the episode when Deb discovers
Quinn's girlfriend is actually Trinity's estranged

00:06:11.379 --> 00:06:16.720
daughter, and the one who killed Deb's boss
and lover, Special Agent Frank Lundy.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:20.470
It's one of the most tense episodes of the
series, and that's why it's one of the best.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:26.520
The introduction of Dr. Evelyn Vogel in the
show's final season undoes much of what we

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:29.330
thought we knew about Dexter and Harry Morgan.

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:34.460
We find out that Dr. Vogel knew Harry and
helped him develop the code that shapes Dexter,

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:37.979
making Dr. Vogel Dexter's spiritual mother.

00:06:37.979 --> 00:06:42.370
The episode goes on to reveal that the Brain
Surgeon is actually Dr. Vogel's son, who faked

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:47.610
his own death as a teenager and has been living
under the name Oliver Saxon.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:51.919
When Dexter pulls a fast one and tries to
trap the Brain Surgeon, Saxon gets away.

00:06:51.919 --> 00:06:56.039
By the end of the episode, we learn that Dr.
Vogel might've been working with Saxon all

00:06:56.039 --> 00:06:58.569
along, a double cross that doesn't make sense.

00:06:58.569 --> 00:07:02.219
This is one of the show's weakest episodes,
when it should be one of the strongest.

00:07:03.221 --> 00:07:05.720
John Lithgow's tour-de-force performance as

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.820
the Trinity Killer hits several high notes
in this episode.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:13.669
In order to figure out just how such a prolific
serial killer could also be an exceptional

00:07:13.669 --> 00:07:16.710
family man, Dexter stalks Arthur Mitchell.

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:22.099
In the process, Dexter finds out that Arthur
is violent and abusive toward his family behind

00:07:22.099 --> 00:07:23.800
closed doors.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:27.480
Dexter begins to regret saving Arthur when
he tries to kill himself.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:31.610
Little does Dexter know, he'll regret a whole
lot more before this season is up.

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:36.550
"Hungry Man" features a key Thanksgiving dinner
where Rita ends up kissing their neighbor,

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:38.970
Elliot, which turns into its own drama.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:44.890
While Rita is kissing Elliot, Dexter is pretending
to be Kyle Butler at Arthur Mitchell's house.

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:49.069
He gets into a confrontation with Arthur as
he tries to protect the Mitchells after Arthur

00:07:49.069 --> 00:07:52.409
breaks his son's finger for damaging his car.

00:07:52.409 --> 00:07:56.460
It's a harrowing, tightly-written episode
that hints at the devastation the season's

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:57.490
finale will bring.

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:03.630
The penultimate episode of "Dexter" is a shocker,
but not in a good way.

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:07.490
Calling back to the show's popular Trinity
Killer arc, Dexter attempts to double cross

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:10.500
Oliver Saxon by pretending to be on his side.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:15.639
It almost works, but what does Dexter do instead
of killing the man he's been hunting this

00:08:15.639 --> 00:08:17.430
entire season?

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:20.970
He leaves him alive and calls Deb to arrest
him instead.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:26.270
Saxon manages to stab Clayton the bounty hunter,
steal his gun, then shoot Deb square in the

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:27.270
stomach.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:30.949
It's a terrible way to end the story of Debra
Morgan, one of the show's most fascinating

00:08:30.949 --> 00:08:32.480
and three-dimensional characters.

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:37.700
From the very beginning, the one person who
suspects Dexter Morgan is hiding a terrible

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.570
secret under his personable veneer is Sergeant
James Doakes.

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:47.140
By Episode 9 of Season 2, Doakes finally figures
it all out: Dexter Morgan is the Bay Harbor

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:48.140
Butcher.

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:52.300
But, like almost everyone who figures out
the truth about Dexter, Doakes leaves just

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:55.050
enough evidence behind for Dexter to spin.

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:59.140
In this case, Dexter's trophy blood slides
in the trunk of Doakes' car makes room for

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:01.870
Miami Metro to suspect Doakes.

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:05.810
While Doakes proves to be one of the most
brilliant characters on the show, being the

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:11.040
first to ID Dexter, this hour marks the beginning
of Doakes' untimely end.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:16.000
The tension between Dexter and Doakes is extraordinary
by this point, and the plot twists are orchestrated

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:17.030
for maximum effect.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:23.260
The Vogel and Saxon drama continues in this
episode, as Dr. Vogel tries to rein in her

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:24.820
psychopathic son.

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:28.930
The traumas that turned young Daniel Vogel
into the Brain Surgeon are revealed, which

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:33.860
land oddly when counterbalanced by Dexter
planning to move to Argentina with Hannah

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:35.350
and Harrison.

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:39.630
Things get especially weird when Hannah, who
still looks exactly the same as her wanted

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:43.010
poster, is recognized by a receptionist at
a hospital.

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:47.339
Yes, this increases the tension, but in an
annoying way that makes you shake your head,

00:09:47.339 --> 00:09:50.390
rather than feel nervous for Dexter and his
family.

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:55.250
In the meantime, the Deb-and-Quinn drama continues
as Quinn breaks up with Jamie, who verbally

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:58.170
assaults Deb right in the middle of Miami
Metro.

00:09:58.170 --> 00:09:59.360
It's embarrassing to watch.

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:05.339
Sergeant Doakes may have died at the end of
Season 2, but his ghost remains very much

00:10:05.339 --> 00:10:10.529
present, especially once LaGuerta's suspicions
about Dexter start to bear fruit.

00:10:10.529 --> 00:10:15.980
Doakes died with people believing he was the
Bay Harbor Butcher, and LaGuerta sees a much-desired

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:21.110
opportunity to clear his name when Dexter
goes after Hector Estrada, another key player

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:23.070
in his mother's murder.

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:27.860
Dexter concocts an elaborate plan to frame
Estrada for LaGuerta's murder.

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:32.010
In this heart-pounding finale, Deb figures
out Dexter's plan and arrives just in time

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:34.760
for LaGuerta to wake up from the sedative.

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:38.070
She begs Deb to kill Dexter, or arrest him.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:42.160
But since Deb's feelings for Dexter have been
revealed to be much more complicated than

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:47.490
a sister's simple love for her adopted brother,
she instead saves Dexter and murders innocent

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:49.040
LaGuerta in cold blood.

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.040
"Who is Deb now?

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:52.620
Who am I?

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:57.470
Is this a new beginning, or the beginning
of the end?"

00:10:58.168 --> 00:11:04.070
The series finale is consistently listed as
one of the worst endings of all time.

00:11:04.070 --> 00:11:08.730
Instead of being able to say a proper goodbye
to "Dexter," we spend this last hour watching

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:10.370
Deb die.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:14.980
After trying to kill Deb once more in the
hospital, Saxon is arrested, and Dexter proceeds

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:18.040
to kill him in the police station with a pen.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:22.639
Dexter sends Hannah off with his son to Buenos
Aires, where he insists he will meet them.

00:11:22.639 --> 00:11:27.180
All the while, a huge hurricane approaches
Miami, prompting Dexter to take Deb off life

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:32.680
support and dump her body where he used to
unload his kills before riding into the storm.

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:34.519
Absolutely none of this makes sense.

00:11:34.519 --> 00:11:38.470
The last we see of Dexter finds him living
as a lumberjack in Oregon.

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:43.040
It's a dreadful and unsatisfying ending for
everyone's favorite antihero.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:46.470
But then again, should serial killers get
happy endings?

